          ],
          "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 7 | Part-II"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.187,
            0.088,
            0.847,
            0.144
          ],
          "content": "Yes, we can use 10 coins of +13 pibs and 5 coins of – 9 pibs to make a total of + 85. Using the two denominations, try to get the following totals:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.188,
            0.151,
            0.603,
            0.171
          ],
          "content": "(a)\t + 20 (b)\t + 40"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.189,
            0.176,
            0.593,
            0.196
          ],
          "content": "(c) $- 5 0$ (d) $+   8$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.189,
            0.201,
            0.591,
            0.221
          ],
          "content": "(e) $+ 1 0$ (f ) $- 2$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.19,
            0.226,
            0.266,
            0.246
          ],
          "content": "(g)\t + 1"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.25,
            0.721,
            0.271
          ],
          "content": "[**Hint:** Writing down a few multiples of 13 and 9 can help.]"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.188,
            0.28,
            0.755,
            0.301
          ],
          "content": "(h) Is it possible to purchase an item that costs 1568 pibs?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.828,
            0.261,
            0.929,
            0.317
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_20_image_8.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.154,
            0.311,
            0.821,
            0.382
          ],
          "content": "11. Find the values of: (a)\t (32 × (– 18)) ÷ ((– 36)) (b)\t (32 ) ÷ ((– 36) × (– 18)) (c)\t (25 × (– 12)) ÷ ((45) × (– 27)) (d)\t (280 × (– 7)) ÷ ((– 8) × (– 35))"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.392,
            0.743,
            0.486
          ],
          "content": "12. Arrange the expressions given below in increasing order. (a)\t (– 348) + (– 1064) (b)\t (– 348) – (– 1064) (c)\t 348 – (– 1064) (d)\t (– 348) × (– 1064) (e)\t 348 × (– 1064) (f) 348 × 964"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.496,
            0.715,
            0.566
          ],
          "content": "13. Given that (– 548) × 972 = – 532656, write the values of: (a)\t (– 547) × 972 (b)\t (– 548) × 971 (c)\t (– 547) × 971"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.576,
            0.846,
            0.615
          ],
          "content": "14. Given that $207 \\times (-33+7) = -5382$ write the value of – 207 × (33 – 7) ="
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.62,
            0.847,
            0.678
          ],
          "content": "15. Use the numbers 3, – 2, 5, – 6 exactly once and the operations ‘+’, ‘–’, and ‘×’ exactly once and brackets as necessary to write an expression such that —"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.188,
            0.684,
            0.578,
            0.703
          ],
          "content": "(a) the result is the maximum possible"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.188,
            0.703,
            0.576,
            0.722
          ],
          "content": "(b) the result is the minimum possible"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.728,
            0.755,
            0.747
          ],
          "content": "16. Fill in the blanks in at least 5 different ways with integers:"
